<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Restore full photos' }) %>
<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Restore full photos</h1>
  <div class="page-actions"><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/newsletter/preview">Back to the preview</a></div>
</div>

<div class="card card-narrow">
  <h2>Why some photos look cut off</h2>
  <p class="muted">Until 15 October 2026 the panel trimmed every uploaded photo to a 4:3 rectangle, keeping the top -
  so in portrait shots the bottom (often the people) was cut off, and only the trimmed copy was saved. New uploads
  are never trimmed any more.</p>

  <h2>Bring the full photos back</h2>
  <p class="muted">Select the <strong>original photos</strong> - from your computer, phone or a Google Drive / WhatsApp
  download - several or all at once, in any order. Each one is <strong>matched automatically</strong> to the trimmed
  photo it came from in this week&#39;s or an upcoming issue, and that photo is swapped for the full version in the
  same place. Pictures that match nothing are skipped and listed, so nothing is ever guessed. Your browser shrinks each
  photo before sending, so big originals upload quickly.</p>
  <form id="photo-restore">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
    <label>Original photos (select them all at once)
      <input type="file" name="photos" accept="image/*" multiple>
    </label>
    <div class="btn-row"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Restore photos</button></div>
  </form>
  <div id="photo-restore-log" style="margin-top:14px; font-size:13.5px; max-height:420px; overflow-y:auto;"></div>
  <p class="muted">Then check the <a href="/newsletter/preview">Preview</a>. If this week&#39;s Mailchimp draft was already
  generated, press <strong>Generate Mailchimp draft</strong> there again so the draft gets the full photos.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
